നാല് slot bounded composition family-യിൽ one-based lexicographic rank തുറക്കുന്ന clean Stage 1 പരിശോധന.

Hamlet, total സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Juliet, lo സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, hi സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, rank സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Macbeth, x സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Lady Macbeth, y സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ophelia, z സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Cordelia, w സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Portia, accepted count സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Viola, capture flag സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ariel, selected x സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Caliban, selected y സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Shylock, selected z സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Horatio, selected w സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, input-output സഹായിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: lexicographic scan-ൽ rank-ാം member capture ചെയ്യുന്നു.

Scene I: total, lo, hi, rank വായിക്കുന്നു.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Juliet]
Prospero:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero:
 Listen to your heart.

Scene II: count=0, capture=0, x=lo.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Portia]
Prospero:
 You are nothing.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Viola]
Prospero:
 You are nothing.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Juliet and Macbeth]
Juliet:
 You are as good as myself.

Scene III: x>hi ആണെങ്കിൽ output.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Macbeth and Romeo]
Macbeth:
 Are you better than Romeo?
 If so, let us proceed to scene XVII.

Scene IV: y=lo.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Juliet and Lady Macbeth]
Juliet:
 You are as good as myself.

Scene V: y>hi ആണെങ്കിൽ x കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Lady Macbeth and Romeo]
Lady Macbeth:
 Are you better than Romeo?
 If so, let us proceed to scene XVI.

Scene VI: z=lo.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Juliet and Ophelia]
Juliet:
 You are as good as myself.

Scene VII: z>hi ആണെങ്കിൽ y കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Ophelia and Romeo]
Ophelia:
 Are you better than Romeo?
 If so, let us proceed to scene XV.

Scene VIII: w=total-x-y-z.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Cordelia]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between Hamlet and Macbeth.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and Lady Macbeth.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and Ophelia.

Scene IX: w പരിധിക്കു പുറത്താണെങ്കിൽ അടുത്ത z.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Cordelia and Juliet]
Cordelia:
 Are you worse than Juliet?
 If so, let us proceed to scene XIV.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Cordelia and Romeo]
Cordelia:
 Are you better than Romeo?
 If so, let us proceed to scene XIV.

Scene X: accepted count കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Portia]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.

Scene XI: capture ചെയ്തിട്ടുണ്ടെങ്കിൽ അടുത്ത z.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Viola and Prospero]
Viola:
 Am I better than nothing?
Prospero:
 If so, let us proceed to scene XIV.

Scene XII: count==rank ആണെങ്കിൽ നാലു ഭാഗങ്ങളും capture ചെയ്യുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Portia and Othello]
Portia:
 Am I as good as you?
Othello:
 If so, let us proceed to scene XIII.
 Let us proceed to scene XIV.

Scene XIII: capture flag.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Viola]
Prospero:
 You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Macbeth and Ariel]
Macbeth:
 You are as good as myself.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Lady Macbeth and Caliban]
Lady Macbeth:
 You are as good as myself.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Ophelia and Shylock]
Ophelia:
 You are as good as myself.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Cordelia and Horatio]
Cordelia:
 You are as good as myself.

Scene XIV: z കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Let us return to scene VII.

Scene XV: y കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Let us return to scene V.

Scene XVI: x കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Macbeth]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Let us return to scene III.

Scene XVII: exact count-ും selected member-ും പുറത്തിടുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Portia]
Prospero:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ariel]
Prospero:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Caliban]
Prospero:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Shylock]
Prospero:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Horatio]
Prospero:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
